  "claim": "Margaret Court won the singles title at a professional tennis tournament held at a Los Angeles arena designed by architect Charles Luckman.",
  "evidencia": "Page: 1973 British Motor Cars of Los Angeles. Sentence: The 1973 British Motor Cars of Los Angeles was a women's tennis tournament played on indoor carpet courts at the The Forum in Los Angeles, California in the United States that was part of the 1973 Virginia Slims World Championship Series.\nPage: 1973 British Motor Cars of Los Angeles. Sentence: The final was watched by 2,693 spectators who saw first-seeded Margaret Court win the singles title and earn $6,000 first-prize money.\nPage: The Forum (Inglewood, California). Sentence: The Forum is a multi-purpose indoor arena in Inglewood, California, adjacent to Los Angeles.\nPage: The Forum (Inglewood, California). Sentence: Architect Charles Luckman's vision was brought to life by engineers Carl Johnson and Svend Nielsen, who were able to engineer the structure so that it had no major support pillars.",
  "evidence_text": "Page: 1973 British Motor Cars of Los Angeles. Sentence: The 1973 British Motor Cars of Los Angeles was a women's tennis tournament played on indoor carpet courts at the The Forum in Los Angeles, California in the United States that was part of the 1973 Virginia Slims World Championship Series.\nPage: 1973 British Motor Cars of Los Angeles. Sentence: The final was watched by 2,693 spectators who saw first-seeded Margaret Court win the singles title and earn $6,000 first-prize money.\nPage: The Forum (Inglewood, California). Sentence: The Forum is a multi-purpose indoor arena in Inglewood, California, adjacent to Los Angeles.\nPage: The Forum (Inglewood, California). Sentence: Architect Charles Luckman's vision was brought to life by engineers Carl Johnson and Svend Nielsen, who were able to engineer the structure so that it had no major support pillars.",
