        "original_id": "b099571a-fa84-5573-9b39-fcbee7d850ef",
        "text": "This chunk is about:\n- Events: 1973 British Motor Cars of Los Angeles\n- Places: The Forum, Inglewood, Los Angeles, California, United States\n- People: Margaret Court, Charles Luckman, Carl Johnson, Svend Nielsen\n- Organizations: 1973 Virginia Slims World Championship Series\n- Topics: women's tennis, indoor carpet courts, arena architecture\n\nFacts:\n- The 1973 British Motor Cars of Los Angeles was a women's tennis tournament in the 1973 Virginia Slims World Championship Series.\n- The 1973 British Motor Cars of Los Angeles was played on indoor carpet courts at The Forum in the Los Angeles area of California, United States.\n- The final of the 1973 British Motor Cars of Los Angeles drew 2,693 spectators.\n- Margaret Court, the first seed, won the singles title at the 1973 British Motor Cars of Los Angeles and earned $6,000 in first-prize money.\n- The Forum is a multi-purpose indoor arena in Inglewood, California, adjacent to Los Angeles.\n- Charles Luckman designed The Forum, and engineers Carl Johnson and Svend Nielsen realized the vision with a structure that had no major support pillars.",
